{"title":"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Step_1:_Finding_some_promising_bound\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Step 1: Finding some promising bound</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Step_2:_Showing_one_solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Step 2: Showing one solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Step_3:_Proving_the_optimality_of_our_solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Step 3: Proving the optimality of our solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Conclusion\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Conclusion</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b28547efd22be1c4a05fa193cd7038fc65d71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are chosen so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5ba70df5a2f9630194f32f50010cd2e78318c98d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;b&lt;c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" />, and the system of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equation\" title=\"Equation\">equations</a>\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/6/706aa31c279b4f4744165bfddf5f8bd451518a57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + y = 2003 \\quad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57c363455cd9e9bf8c2dceadb7298327d953e0bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\quad y = |x-a| + |x-b| + |x-c|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"246\" height=\"18\" /></center>\n<p>has exactly one solution. What is the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/a/5aa9d96a7d1137dd942927f22127fe275458bac7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 668 \\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 669 \\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 1002 \\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 2003 \\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 2004$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"460\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fc742e57cf5fc67693f8df6262cde7a96b0ef98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=|x-a|+|x-b|+|x-c|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"255\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/9/db9a42be377d9781da67c3347a3d3a1ddc69e5c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"10\" />, the slope is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31b51deaa1a9e903d120a02141556c3e70e348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/2/ea200ce05e8129b1169b9e90372236816ee2219a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;x&lt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />, the slope is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/2/a92fd4b010b17c5ce65c84909e9a54e986e3f7c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&lt;x&lt;c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />, the slope is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/a/59ab5c98496a83ed16e5b8ccc07d73beaae93fcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&lt;x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"10\" />, the slope is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741720281e465fc7461c32d504f6d54c5bcaff7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b7a7453263a8fb2e47b318afc336a9db8935621.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=|b-a|+|b-b|+|b-c|=c-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"287\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/0/b70e6301769eaad173a5d094159ec7fee880b649.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b,c-a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> is a point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />. In fact, it is the minimum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> considering the slope of lines to the left and right of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/0/b70e6301769eaad173a5d094159ec7fee880b649.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b,c-a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, graphing this will produce a figure that looks like a cup:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa926b12d0a7c803d530009612b24aae9cbe456c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph; size(100); draw((0,6)--(3,0)); xaxis(0,8.5); yaxis(0,10); real f(real x) { return -3(x-2)+5; } real f2(real x) { return -1(x-2)+5; } real f3(real x) { return 1(x-4)+3; } real f4(real x) { return 3(x-7)+6; } draw(graph(f,0,2)); draw(graph(f2,2,4)); draw(graph(f3,4,7)); draw(graph(f4,7,8.5)); draw((2,-0.25)--(2,0.25)); label(&quot;a&quot;,(2,0),N); draw((4,-0.25)--(4,0.25)); label(&quot;b&quot;,(4,0),N); draw((7,-0.25)--(7,0.25)); label(&quot;c&quot;,(7,0),N); dot((2,5)); label(&quot;P&quot;,(1.9,5.2),E); [/asy]\" width=\"128\" height=\"168\" />\nFrom the graph, it is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/a/5daffd02eb1112367cdeee413853763c4a093106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x+y=2003$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" /> have one intersection point if and only if they intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed47ef35959c171399e8f18eed4b517223823c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a$\" width=\"44\" height=\"8\" />. Since the line where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/2/ea200ce05e8129b1169b9e90372236816ee2219a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;x&lt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" /> has slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, the positive difference in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinates from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed47ef35959c171399e8f18eed4b517223823c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a$\" width=\"44\" height=\"8\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741720281e465fc7461c32d504f6d54c5bcaff7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/c/02c60c151331e235dc6d9df7ca403b6f0c9af39b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />. Together with the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/0/b70e6301769eaad173a5d094159ec7fee880b649.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b,c-a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/0/02060b20d1316a52b062f9de731f53c458e54b7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=(a,c-a+b-a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"170\" height=\"18\" />. Since this point is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed47ef35959c171399e8f18eed4b517223823c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a$\" width=\"44\" height=\"8\" />, the only intersection point with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/a/5daffd02eb1112367cdeee413853763c4a093106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x+y=2003$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/1/e41a7b74dee93566aa6911bfa3c64c586e9cebc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot a+(b+c-2a)=2003 \\implies b+c=2003$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"354\" height=\"18\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/3/c23f82ed147584a2ffb37aa3f77dcd2542d16ce2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&gt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />, the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/f/40f37787765da37aa2a891a87836737d928a2ae7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=1001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45e533ef700405599bc93e10d0835e25c78b6ff8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=1002$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />. This is indeed a solution as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/e/8becb83d37f49e4f7485ec5a53d66d441b6a4068.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" /> puts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a77b269dab2cab9fac4604af5272ea43009b648d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=2003-2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"17\" />, and thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3fd47e6a3e448ac2c22260fd32aef92052be914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 1002}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"81\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p>This indeed works for the two right segments of slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We already know that the minimum is achieved between slopes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31b51deaa1a9e903d120a02141556c3e70e348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/9/1f9563360f04d9b959c980b16bef6f5a9be58615.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+c=2003$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"97\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/c/60ce45b15f94619b4a40fcf5fb9d16a77b44fbeb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2003-2x=-a-b+c+x\\longrightarrow 3x\\ne a+b-c+2003 \\{b&lt;x&lt;c\\}\\rightarrow (3b,3c)\\ne a+2b\\rightarrow b&gt;a\\text{ (true)}\\]\" width=\"731\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/7/f97e8d6374b16f6fa9ff4730103ae71da24bc489.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2003-2x=-a-b-c+3x\\longrightarrow 5x\\ne a+b+c+2003 \\{x&gt;c\\}\\rightarrow (5c,+5\\infty)\\ne a+2b+2c\\rightarrow 3c&gt;a+2b\\text{ (true)}\\]\" width=\"804\" height=\"18\" />\nIndeed, within the restricted domain of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in each segment, these inequalities prove to be unequal everywhere. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a77b269dab2cab9fac4604af5272ea43009b648d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=2003-2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"17\" /> is strictly below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/0/a80145e0c4f74ada4f4b55f9273565d9e53cb6b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=|x-a|+|x-b|+|x-c|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"234\" height=\"20\" /> at these domains.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Step_1:_Finding_some_promising_bound\">Step 1: Finding some promising bound</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Step 1: Finding some promising bound\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Does the system have a solution where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/7/12789c7998bd4728e0105e048101cc230435907d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\leq a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />? \n</p><p>For such a solution we would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/3/b337cc6cb6a1b6d3f3289897ed4c0c7fb35151e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=(a-x)+(b-x)+(c-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"242\" height=\"18\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/7042c723c849257d8c09888bde6861d1d8664fcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x+(a+b+c-3x)=2003$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"227\" height=\"18\" />, which solves to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/4865be686dbcd2ce1db1982692358e4d6d7fa3d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a+b+c-2003$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"162\" height=\"14\" />.\nIf we want to avoid this solution, we need to have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65f61cc6a1236f3fecd0ebd5dd964268c3519ee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c-2003&gt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"162\" height=\"14\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a34f13e9b258824cdce703e9e309af540b28f6d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+c&gt;2003$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/5/5051d880af458f8cc7426d804e7a64ab5d73bb1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c\\geq 1003$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" />. \nIn other words, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/1/681a3aae9f39d8f112761fdac24f0b1c9faf7c3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&lt;1003$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />, there will always be one solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/7/12789c7998bd4728e0105e048101cc230435907d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\leq a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Step_2:_Showing_one_solution\">Step 2: Showing one solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Step 2: Showing one solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We will now find out whether there is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/1/681a3aae9f39d8f112761fdac24f0b1c9faf7c3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&lt;1003$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" /> for which (and some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" />) the system has only one solution. We already know of one such solution, so we need to make sure that no other solution appears.\n</p><p>Obviously, there are three more theoretically possible solutions: one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/8/c28d39d206246ca7566d0b820e2edbaf10b03954.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(a,b\\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />, one in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/b/b2bd1fa23107f95ab25b8af850d1a9cbe06fb4f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(b,c\\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" />, and one in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/2/6f2f0195c6a11fde5c8936f582e24ba1a43ec931.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(c,\\infty\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" />.\nThe first case solves to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/3/3f3ee64fce8c2f871ed428dce9abb5c1a1c46a6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2003+a-b-c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"163\" height=\"14\" />, the second to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/40591530da10ae8caabf5f03af6b5cefd7a0e09b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x=2003+a+b-c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"172\" height=\"14\" />, and the third to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/c/67ce166b17a1d831a6698a393a6eb47c246cda89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x=2003+a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"172\" height=\"14\" />.\nWe need to make sure that the following three conditions hold:\n</p>\n<ol><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/2/022e91231cc77178d5ba4e61fa35c2a27923a9b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003+a-b-c\\not\\in\\left(a,b\\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"186\" height=\"18\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/804aa269eadb95229dc6e152077369195e252a2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2003+a+b-c}3\\not\\in \\left(b,c\\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"188\" height=\"37\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/8/bf81c9a73a2707f651c556c464d3fb2bedca150d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2003+a+b+c}5\\not\\in\\left(c,\\infty\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"201\" height=\"37\" />.</li></ol>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45e533ef700405599bc93e10d0835e25c78b6ff8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=1002$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/f/40f37787765da37aa2a891a87836737d928a2ae7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=1001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />. We then have:\n</p>\n<ol><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/85006a5902f778467406e45a0e4b7c4b35657d91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003+a-b-c=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"162\" height=\"14\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/3/1a3a8d88298ad9c9e82c0cfc0eb062850bb3e8bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2003+a+b-c}3 = \\frac{2002+a}3 \\leq \\frac{2002+1000}3 &lt; 1001 = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"444\" height=\"37\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/a/fcab9ac4078d2611b0ae859e5c1be70ba3ab58c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2003+a+b+c}5 = \\frac{4006+a}5 \\leq \\frac{4006+1006}5 &lt; 1002 = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"446\" height=\"37\" /></li></ol>\n<p>Hence for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45e533ef700405599bc93e10d0835e25c78b6ff8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=1002$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/f/40f37787765da37aa2a891a87836737d928a2ae7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=1001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" /> and any valid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> the system has exactly one solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/a/5fa50c4b84159ae00e8bd2a4e548d715deaff231.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)=(a,2003-2a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Step_3:_Proving_the_optimality_of_our_solution\">Step 3: Proving the optimality of our solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Step 3: Proving the optimality of our solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We will now show that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/56334c2b30fd67a232c785e26bd8f4ac97d9e4fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&lt;1002$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" /> the system always has a solution such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49cc074e4377ef012b7ae84a6b96debec486e2ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"10\" />. This will mean that the system has at least two solutions, and thus the solution with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45e533ef700405599bc93e10d0835e25c78b6ff8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=1002$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" /> is optimal.\n</p>\n<ol><li>As we are looking for a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/56334c2b30fd67a232c785e26bd8f4ac97d9e4fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&lt;1002$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/4/ab4764c902e50c1aff98fae8a305c58a2467c90c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+c\\leq 2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"17\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/9/fe9d7f924f53d729bee984a79047687cdb4e5b50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003+a-b-c &gt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"162\" height=\"14\" />. To make sure that the value falls outside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/8/c28d39d206246ca7566d0b820e2edbaf10b03954.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(a,b\\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />, we need to make it larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/b/f9b0aca3860ca9c54d4bb9b14c6be54083641945.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003+a-b-c &gt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"160\" height=\"14\" />, or equivalently <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/2/ea20c99856f5c91a5c8d26045f6460e51e517ab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003+a &gt; 2b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"139\" height=\"14\" />.</li>\n<li>The condition we just derived, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/2/ea20c99856f5c91a5c8d26045f6460e51e517ab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003+a &gt; 2b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"139\" height=\"14\" />, can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/c/0bcb59b4b55afd3c3c378cef7947301f4fc7f39e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003+a+b &gt; 3b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"169\" height=\"14\" />, then as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a009ecae18525ec4832029b467d7a1f9f077187.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003+a+b-c &gt; 3b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"169\" height=\"14\" />, which becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/0/58002d9ca16e67f6fc8b3bd5f850585156450efd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2003+a+b-c}3 &gt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"164\" height=\"37\" />. Thus to make sure that the second value falls outside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/b/b2bd1fa23107f95ab25b8af850d1a9cbe06fb4f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(b,c\\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" />, we need to make it larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. The inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22baffbc816204d4136f6306c20b0084cf09fb09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2003+a+b-c}3 &gt; c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"164\" height=\"37\" /> simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f01332350020fd2d685f719c3a8a5e62a8adcd30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003+a+b &gt; 4c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"139\" height=\"14\" />.</li>\n<li>To avoid the last solution, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afa85b663fe5a0ad7d3cff5f99c8465e35e7e8c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2003+a+b+c}5\\leq c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"166\" height=\"39\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5ea6db4de7297ab0caed65f492f0b8c7fe72dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003+a+b \\leq 4c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"15\" />.</li></ol>\n<p>The last two inequalities contradict each other, thus there are no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> that would satisfy both of them.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Conclusion\">Conclusion</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Conclusion\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We just showed that whenever <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/56334c2b30fd67a232c785e26bd8f4ac97d9e4fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&lt;1002$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />, the system has at least two different solutions: one with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/7/12789c7998bd4728e0105e048101cc230435907d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\leq a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and one with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49cc074e4377ef012b7ae84a6b96debec486e2ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p>We also showed that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45e533ef700405599bc93e10d0835e25c78b6ff8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=1002$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" /> there are some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> for which the system has exactly one solution. \n</p><p>Hence the optimal value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3fd47e6a3e448ac2c22260fd32aef92052be914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 1002}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"81\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B\">2003 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Pro